From 316490b97311af6daebe80b5bad6877b99bbe6d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:25:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/32] test(qsa): GPU correctness test for the widened pending
 ring

Runs on a spare device with arbitrary tensors. Checks that the in-CUDA-graph
Triton row-metadata kernel reproduces the eager slot builders for every ring size
(this is what validates the new RING constexpr, since the graph path recomputes
the addressing on device), that one W=8 forward writes bitwise-identical
compressed keys to two sequential W=4 forwards, and that the historical
ratio-sized ring does NOT reproduce them -- so a green run cannot be mistaken for
"the ring size did not matter".

The fused compress-store leg is best-effort and skips when the JIT toolchain is
absent; it is not what this patch changes.
